  "title": "Answer: experience is measurable in principle",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "b34eb88a-2d55-4c3b-947a-399f93a2d428",
      "text": "Because experience has a mathematical object isomorphic to it, its properties can be measured. Valence is a crisp quantity to which a measure applies, read in practice through proxies such as harmonic consonance and signal compressibility.",
